# 🤖 Jarvis AI — Desktop Voice & Text Assistant

A modern, multi-functional desktop assistant built with Python and Tkinter. **Jarvis** integrates real-time AI capabilities powered by Google's Gemini API, complete with voice recognition, speech synthesis, system automation, and an intuitive dark-themed GUI.

---

## ✨ Features

* **🧠 AI Intelligence (Google Gemini)**: Ask questions, summarize text, explain concepts, or generate code snippets instantly using `gemini-2.5-flash`.
* **🎙️ Dual Input Modes**: Interact seamlessly via direct text input or hands-free voice commands.
* **🗣️ Text-to-Speech (TTS)**: Voice responses powered by `gTTS` and `pyttsx3` with customizable volume, Hindi/English language switching, and male/female voice options.
* **🖥️ System Control**:
  * Lock screen, shutdown, or restart your PC via voice commands.
  * Adjust or mute/unmute system volume.
  * Launch apps, open file directories, or set desktop wallpapers.
* **🌐 Web & Media Integration**:
  * Play songs on YouTube or Spotify.
  * Open quick web links (Google, YouTube, Cricbuzz, social media).
  * Pause/Resume video playback hands-free.
* **⏰ Productivity Tools**:
  * Set desktop alarms and time-based reminders.
  * Fetch live top news headlines (India/Global).
  * Extract and read PDF content out loud using PyMuPDF.
  * Capture instant photos using your device camera.
* **📜 Conversation History**: Local session logging to view and clear past interactions.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **GUI Framework**: Python `tkinter` (Custom styled components)
* **AI Model**: Google GenAI SDK (`google-genai`)
* **Voice & Audio**: `SpeechRecognition`, `gTTS`, `pyttsx3`, `pygame`
* **Media & Systems**: `opencv-python`, `pyautogui`, `fitz` (PyMuPDF), `pywhatkit`, `requests`

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

### 1. Prerequisites
Ensure you have **Python 3.10+** installed on your system.

### 2. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone [https://github.com/your-username/jarvis-assistant.git](https://github.com/your-username/jarvis-assistant.git)
cd jarvis-assistant
